theorem a-recursion-header-and-an-assumption
  note        An assumption below a define by recursion in the statement
              speaks of its sequence, written out as the conclusion is.
  let F(0) = 0,  F(k + 1) = F(k) + 1,  for k ∈ ℕ₀                     (D1)
         reads the counting sequence
  assume F(1) = 2                                                     (H1)
  then F(1) + 1 = 3

1.  F(1) + 1 = 2 + 1
    substitute F(1) = 2 (H1)

2.  F(1) + 1 = 3
    calculation
      F(1) + 1 = 2 + 1     1
               = 3         arithmetic
